From: brainux-pw-a9300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: brain_defconfig: reserve 4 MiB of CMA, and name the release

Without CMA, a DRM dumb buffer comes straight from the page allocator.
The 480x320 RGB565 frame of brain-lq050j1ug01 is 300 KiB, an order-7
allocation, and drm_gem_dma_create() asks with __GFP_NOWARN. Right
after boot, with 128 MiB of RAM and everything starting at once, it
can fail silently: Xorg's modesetting driver then stops with
"AddScreen/ScreenInit failed for driver 0", and /proc/vmstat shows
compact_fail with no compact_success. Logging in again a few minutes
later worked.

Reserve 4 MiB of CMA for such buffers. The page allocator still uses
the area for movable pages while nobody needs it.

CMA changes the symbol versions, so modules built for the kernel
without it refuse to load ("disagrees about version of symbol"). Set
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION to -pwa9300, so the release (and the modules
directory) differs from the kernel without CMA and both can stay
installed.

diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/brain_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/brain_defconfig
--- a/arch/arm/configs/brain_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/brain_defconfig
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-pwa9300"
 CONFIG_SYSVIPC=y
 CONFIG_NO_HZ=y
 CONFIG_HIGH_RES_TIMERS=y
@@ -27,6 +28,7 @@
 CONFIG_ZSWAP=y
 CONFIG_Z3FOLD=y
 # CONFIG_COMPAT_BRK is not set
+CONFIG_CMA=y
 CONFIG_NET=y
 CONFIG_PACKET=y
 CONFIG_UNIX=y
@@ -216,6 +218,8 @@
 CONFIG_NLS_ISO8859_1=y
 CONFIG_NLS_ISO8859_15=y
 CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_MXS_DCP=y
+CONFIG_DMA_CMA=y
+CONFIG_CMA_SIZE_MBYTES=4
 CONFIG_FONTS=y
 CONFIG_FONT_8x16=y
 CONFIG_FONT_6x11=y
